==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|mere|ly|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈmɪəli/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈmɪɹli/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-merely.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[wholly|Wholly]], [[entirely]]. {{defdate|16th-20th c.}}
#* '''1644''', {{w|John Milton}}, ''Aeropagitica'':
#*: It is not forgot, since the acute and distinct ''Arminius'' was perverted '''meerly''' by the perusing of a namelesse discourse writt'n at ''Delf'', which at first he took in hand to confute.
# {{lb|en|focus}} Without any other reason etc.; [[only]], [[just]], and [[nothing]] [[more]]. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}

